    "notes": [
      "Unlike the original Hausa/Igbo seed lists, no clear errors were found in the original Swahili seed — it was already largely accurate. This upgrade focuses on adding structure, expanding vocabulary, and separating grammatical words from translation targets.",
      "Swahili has genuine, well-established native cybersecurity vocabulary (unlike some other African languages where tech terms are mostly bare English loanwords) — e.g. 'udukuzi' (hacking) and 'programu hasidi' (malware) are real, actively-used terms, not constructed compounds, confirmed via an actual Swahili-language hacking glossary and a security company's Swahili blog."
